Description: Analysis of spatial relationships between cell types in spatial transcriptomics data. Spatial proximity is a critical factor in cell-cell communication. The package calculates nearest neighbor distances between specified cell types and provides visualization tools to explore spatial patterns. Input can be supplied as a plain data frame or directly as a Seurat v5 object or RDS file, with spatial coordinates extracted automatically. For multi-sample datasets, a sample-aware mode restricts nearest-neighbour matching to within-sample comparisons, preventing cross-sample artefacts. Output includes both the distance and the barcode of the nearest target spot for each reference cell, enabling straightforward merging with external metadata. Applications include studying cell-cell interactions, immune microenvironment characterization, and spatial organization of tissues.
